IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr2-helpers`
IMPORT `mlr2-ecdd`
IMPORT `mlr2-sdd-emoney`

-- TESTS for mlr2-sdd-emoney.l4 (regulations 37 and 38).  Every expected value is written by hand from the text beside the
-- assertion; none is copied from the encoding's own output.  Each line is one #ASSERT.

§ `Regulation 37(1) -- the permission`

-- arguments: relevant person (S-8); the determination of the degree of risk; took into account (a) the regulation 18(1) assessment, (b) information under regulations 17(9) and 47, (c) the paragraph (3) risk factors
#ASSERT `reg 37(1) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures` (JUST TRUE) `low risk` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a determination of high risk, or of neither: "if it determines that ... presents a low degree of risk" is not met
#ASSERT `reg 37(1) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures` (JUST TRUE) `high risk` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 37(1) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures` (JUST TRUE) `neither high nor low risk` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- each of the three things "having taken into account" is needed
#ASSERT `reg 37(1) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures` (JUST TRUE) `low risk` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 37(1) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures` (JUST TRUE) `low risk` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 37(1) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures` (JUST TRUE) `low risk` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a relevant person, or regulation 8 not answered: the rule is addressed to "a relevant person"
#ASSERT `reg 37(1) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures` (JUST FALSE) `low risk` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 37(1) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures` NOTHING `low risk` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 37(2) -- what a relevant person that applies simplified measures must do`

#ASSERT `reg 37(2)(a) the relevant person must continue to comply with the requirements in regulations 28, 29 and 30A` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(2)(a) the relevant person must continue to comply with the requirements in regulations 28, 29 and 30A` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 37(2)(a) the relevant person must continue to comply with the requirements in regulations 28, 29 and 30A` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 37(2)(a) the relevant person must continue to comply with the requirements in regulations 28, 29 and 30A` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the permission to adjust: relevant person; applies simplified measures; the measure is one under regulation 28 or 29(11) to (13); the adjustment reflects the paragraph (1) determination
#ASSERT `reg 37(2)(a) the relevant person may adjust the extent, timing or type of the measure` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a measure under any other regulation, or an adjustment that does not reflect the determination: the grant does not reach it
#ASSERT `reg 37(2)(a) the relevant person may adjust the extent, timing or type of the measure` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 37(2)(a) the relevant person may adjust the extent, timing or type of the measure` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 37(2)(a) the relevant person may adjust the extent, timing or type of the measure` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 37(2)(a) the relevant person may adjust the extent, timing or type of the measure` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 37(2)(b) the relevant person must carry out sufficient monitoring of the business relationships or transactions subject to those measures` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(2)(b) the relevant person must carry out sufficient monitoring of the business relationships or transactions subject to those measures` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 37(2)(b) the relevant person must carry out sufficient monitoring of the business relationships or transactions subject to those measures` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 37(3) and (4) -- the risk factors`

-- generated tests for the entries of reg 37(3) (expected wording read from the raw text by line number)
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` `reg 37(3)(a)(i) is a public administration, or a publicly owned enterprise` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` `reg 37(3)(a)(i) is a public administration, or a publicly owned enterprise` EQUALS JUST "is a public administration, or a publicly owned enterprise"
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` `reg 37(3)(a)(ii) is an individual resident in a geographical area of lower risk` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` `reg 37(3)(a)(ii) is an individual resident in a geographical area of lower risk` EQUALS JUST "is an individual resident in a geographical area of lower risk (see sub-paragraph (c))"
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` `reg 37(3)(a)(iii) is a credit institution or a financial institution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` `reg 37(3)(a)(iii) is a credit institution or a financial institution` EQUALS JUST "is a credit institution or a financial institution which is— (aa) subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity (within the meaning of that directive); and (bb) supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive"
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` `reg 37(3)(a)(iv) is a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` `reg 37(3)(a)(iv) is a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market` EQUALS JUST "is a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market, and the location of the regulated market"
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` `reg 37(3)(b)(i) a life insurance policy for which the premium is low` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` `reg 37(3)(b)(i) a life insurance policy for which the premium is low` EQUALS JUST "a life insurance policy for which the premium is low"
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` `reg 37(3)(b)(ii) an insurance policy for a pension scheme which does not provide` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` `reg 37(3)(b)(ii) an insurance policy for a pension scheme which does not provide` EQUALS JUST "an insurance policy for a pension scheme which does not provide for an early surrender option, and cannot be used as collateral"
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` `reg 37(3)(b)(iii) a pension, superannuation or similar scheme which satisfies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` `reg 37(3)(b)(iii) a pension, superannuation or similar scheme which satisfies` EQUALS JUST "a pension, superannuation or similar scheme which satisfies the following conditions— (aa) the scheme provides retirement benefits to employees; (bb) contributions to the scheme are made by way of deductions from wages; and (cc) the scheme rules do not permit the assignment of a member's interest under the scheme"
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` `reg 37(3)(b)(iv) a financial product or service that provides appropriately defined` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` `reg 37(3)(b)(iv) a financial product or service that provides appropriately defined` EQUALS JUST "a financial product or service that provides appropriately defined and limited services to certain types of customers to increase access for financial inclusion purposes in the United Kingdom"
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` `reg 37(3)(b)(v) a product where the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` `reg 37(3)(b)(v) a product where the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing` EQUALS JUST "a product where the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing are managed by other factors such as purse limits or transparency of ownership"
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` `reg 37(3)(b)(vi) a child trust fund within the meaning given by section 1(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` `reg 37(3)(b)(vi) a child trust fund within the meaning given by section 1(2)` EQUALS JUST "a child trust fund within the meaning given by section 1(2) of the Child Trust Funds Act 2004"
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` `reg 37(3)(b)(vii) a junior ISA within the meaning given by regulation 2B` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` `reg 37(3)(b)(vii) a junior ISA within the meaning given by regulation 2B` EQUALS JUST "a junior ISA within the meaning given by regulation 2B of the Individual Savings Account Regulations 1998"
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` `reg 37(3)(c)(i) the United Kingdom` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` `reg 37(3)(c)(i) the United Kingdom` EQUALS JUST "the United Kingdom"
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` `reg 37(3)(c)(ii) a third country which has effective systems to counter money laundering` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` `reg 37(3)(c)(ii) a third country which has effective systems to counter money laundering` EQUALS JUST "a third country which has effective systems to counter money laundering and terrorist financing"
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` `reg 37(3)(c)(iii) a third country identified by credible sources as having a low level` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` `reg 37(3)(c)(iii) a third country identified by credible sources as having a low level` EQUALS JUST "a third country identified by credible sources as having a low level of corruption or other criminal activity, such as terrorism (within the meaning of section 1 of the Terrorism Act 2000 ), money laundering, and the production and supply of illicit drugs"
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` `reg 37(3)(c)(iv) a third country which, on the basis of credible sources` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` `reg 37(3)(c)(iv) a third country which, on the basis of credible sources` EQUALS JUST "a third country which, on the basis of credible sources, such as evaluations, detailed assessment reports or published follow-up reports published by the Financial Action Task Force, the International Monetary Fund, the World Bank, the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development or other international bodies or non-governmental organisations— (aa) has requirements to counter money laundering and terrorist financing that are consistent with the revised Recommendations published by the Financial Action Task Force in February 2012 and updated in October 2016; and (bb) effectively implements those Recommendations"
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` `reg 37(3) another risk factor` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` `reg 37(3) another risk factor` EQUALS NOTHING

-- "When assessing": arguments relevant person; is assessing; the risk factor
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take account of the risk factor when assessing` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `reg 37(3)(c)(i) the United Kingdom` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take account of the risk factor when assessing` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `reg 37(3) another risk factor` EQUALS NOTHING
-- not assessing: "When assessing whether there is a low degree of risk" is not met, so no ("when" counts as "where", ruling of 2026-11-05)
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take account of the risk factor when assessing` (JUST TRUE) FALSE `reg 37(3)(c)(i) the United Kingdom` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take account of the risk factor when assessing` (JUST FALSE) TRUE `reg 37(3)(c)(i) the United Kingdom` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): "may not always indicate" -- nothing, whatever the number of risk factors
#ASSERT `reg 37(4) the presence of the risk factors indicates a low risk of money laundering and terrorist financing` 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 37(4) the presence of the risk factors indicates a low risk of money laundering and terrorist financing` 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 37(4) the presence of the risk factors indicates a low risk of money laundering and terrorist financing` 4 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 37(5) and (6) -- the pooled account`

-- (6): arguments relevant person (S-7); carries on business in a third country; equivalent requirements; supervised equivalently
#ASSERT `reg 37(6) paragraph (5) applies to the person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(6) paragraph (5) applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(6) paragraph (5) applies to the person` NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a third-country person needs both (b)(i) and (b)(ii) and the third country
-- paragraph (5) applies "where the customer is a person to whom paragraph (6) applies": a person in neither (a) nor (b) is outside the class (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); fork F37-1)
#ASSERT `reg 37(6) paragraph (5) applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 37(6) paragraph (5) applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 37(6) paragraph (5) applies to the person` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a third-country firm that is not supervised, and whether it is a relevant person is not answered: nothing
#ASSERT `reg 37(6) paragraph (5) applies to the person` NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 37(6) paragraph (5) applies to the person` NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b)(iii): the three conditions (aa) to (cc)
#ASSERT `reg 37(3)(b)(iii) the scheme satisfies the conditions` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3)(b)(iii) the scheme satisfies the conditions` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3)(b)(iii) the scheme satisfies the conditions` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 37(3)(b)(iii) the scheme satisfies the conditions` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5): arguments relevant person (S-8); paragraph (6) applies to the customer; the product is a pooled account; low degree of risk with the holder; identity information available
#ASSERT `reg 37(5) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures to the pooled account` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 37(5) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures to the pooled account` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 37(5) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures to the pooled account` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 37(5) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures to the pooled account` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 37(5) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures to the pooled account` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- paragraph (6) not answered, everything else met: not answered
#ASSERT `reg 37(5) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures to the pooled account` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 37(5) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures to the pooled account` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 37(8) -- when simplified measures may not be continued`

-- arguments: relevant person; (a) doubts; (b) assessment changes; (c) suspects; (d) the regulation 33(1) answer
#ASSERT `reg 37(8) the relevant person may continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures under paragraph (1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 37(8) the relevant person may continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures under paragraph (1)` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 37(8) the relevant person may continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures under paragraph (1)` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 37(8) the relevant person may continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures under paragraph (1)` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- none of the four cases: the paragraph says nothing of continuing
#ASSERT `reg 37(8) the relevant person may continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures under paragraph (1)` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 37(8) the relevant person may continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures under paragraph (1)` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- a limb that holds settles it although regulation 33(1) is unanswered
#ASSERT `reg 37(8) the relevant person may continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures under paragraph (1)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a relevant person: nothing
#ASSERT `reg 37(8) the relevant person may continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures under paragraph (1)` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 37(8) the relevant person may continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures under paragraph (1)` NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 38(1) -- electronic money: the disapplication`

-- arguments: relevant person; maximum amount stored; not reloadable; monthly limit (MAYBE); UK only; used exclusively for goods or services; anonymous e-money cannot fund it
-- all met, with a payment instrument that is not reloadable: (a) 150 is met, (b)(i) is met
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the relevant person is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 150 TRUE NOTHING FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- boundary of (a): 150 passes (above) and 150.01 does not; 100 passes
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the relevant person is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 100 TRUE NOTHING FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the relevant person is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 150.01 TRUE NOTHING FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b)(ii): reloadable, with a monthly limit of 150 that can only be used in the United Kingdom
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the relevant person is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 150 FALSE (JUST 150) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the relevant person is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 150 FALSE (JUST 150.01) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the relevant person is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 150 FALSE (JUST 149) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b)(ii) fails when the instrument can be used outside the United Kingdom, or when no monthly limit exists
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the relevant person is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 150 FALSE (JUST 150) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the relevant person is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 150 FALSE NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) and (d)
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the relevant person is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 150 TRUE NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the relevant person is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 150 TRUE NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a relevant person: nothing
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the relevant person is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money` (JUST FALSE) 150 TRUE NOTHING FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the relevant person is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money` NOTHING 150 TRUE NOTHING FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- the effect: regulations 27, 28, 30 and 33 to 37 do not apply, and no other regulation is named
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the regulation does not apply in relation to the electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 27 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the regulation does not apply in relation to the electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 28 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the regulation does not apply in relation to the electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the regulation does not apply in relation to the electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 33 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the regulation does not apply in relation to the electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 37 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the regulation does not apply in relation to the electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 29 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the regulation does not apply in relation to the electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 31 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the regulation does not apply in relation to the electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 32 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the regulation does not apply in relation to the electronic money` (JUST TRUE) 38 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the regulation does not apply in relation to the electronic money` (JUST FALSE) 35 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 38(1) the regulation does not apply in relation to the electronic money` NOTHING 35 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 38(2) to (5)`

-- (2): arguments: a cash redemption or withdrawal; the amount redeemed; a remote payment transaction; the amount redeemed per transaction
#ASSERT `reg 38(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the transaction` TRUE 50.01 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 38(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the transaction` TRUE 50 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 38(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the transaction` TRUE 49 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b): a remote payment transaction, judged per transaction
#ASSERT `reg 38(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the transaction` TRUE 40 TRUE 50.01 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 38(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the transaction` TRUE 40 TRUE 50 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the per-transaction figure counts only for remote payment transactions
#ASSERT `reg 38(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the transaction` TRUE 40 FALSE 60 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a redemption or a withdrawal: the paragraph speaks of "any transaction which consists of" those
#ASSERT `reg 38(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the transaction` FALSE 500 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
