#ASSERT `reg 38(4A) the institution may accept payment using the anonymous prepaid card` `casino` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5)(a): payment service provider; contracts with a payee; results in a transfer of funds to the payee
#ASSERT `reg 38(5)(a) the person is an acquirer` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 38(5)(a) the person is an acquirer` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 38(5)(a) the person is an acquirer` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 38(5)(a) the person is an acquirer` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 38(5) the meaning of the term is given by` `reg 38(5)(b) payment instrument` EQUALS "regulation 2(1) of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011"
#ASSERT `reg 38(5) the meaning of the term is given by` `reg 38(5)(c) remote payment transaction` EQUALS "regulation 2 of the Payment Services Regulations 2017"

§ `Regulation 37(8) as a prohibition (SHANT): traces, read by hand`

-- A DEONTIC value cannot be compared with #ASSERT on the main binary, so these traces are READ, not asserted.  Expected from the text
-- ("must not continue to apply"): continuing is a BREACH; no event leaves the prohibition standing.  The decision function above is asserted.
#TRACE `reg 37(8) a relevant person must not continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 37(8) a relevant person` DOES `reg 37(8) continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures under paragraph (1) after a doubt, a change of assessment, a suspicion or a regulation 33(1) condition` AT 3
